# Guardrails — data-boar-site (binds Cursor AND Claude)

Canonical: `docs/adr/ADR-0001` (Proposed → only the HITL Accepts) and `AGENTS.md`. Add guardrails; never remove one.

- **HITL is the sole author.** NEVER add `Co-Authored-By: <tool>` or `Claude-Session:` to a commit message. The operator signs (ed25519). The harness default does not override this.
- **Local gates before push:** `scripts/pre-commit` runs automatically (lint + code-quality + quick anti-regression); run `scripts/check-all.sh` (full suite) **before opening a PR**. Must be green.
- **PR-only to `main`** — no force-push, no branch deletion; the `guardrails` CI check must pass.
- **Evidence, not legal conclusion.** No "guarantees/ensures compliance", no "certifies", no wrong article citations (RIPD ↔ LGPD Art. 38; DPIA ↔ GDPR Art. 35), no "byte a byte" for ML/DL.
- **No LLM decides findings** — the product is deterministic / no generative LLM on the critical path; keep that in the copy.
- **Supply chain:** pin GitHub Actions to a full SHA; allowlist external resources; the form posts only to `api.hsforms.com`.
- **Bilingual pt-BR ↔ en-US**, idiomatic (never mechanical); EN overclaim-safe. Sacred taxonomy exact; minors' data first-class ("inventory & triage signals, never age verification").
- **Site chrome:** never hand-edit one page’s `#site-nav` / `<footer>` — edit `partials/site-chrome/` and run `scripts/sync-site-chrome.py` (see `01-site-chrome.mdc`).
